DXSPIDER WEB ADMIN - OPERATIONAL OVERVIEW
=========================================

DXWeb Admin is the separate SYSOP administration web application. Its
current application version is reported by /admin-version.json. Its
default HTTP port is 7381.

The HTTP listener is configurable with DXWEB_HOST and DXWEB_PORT. Direct
deployments normally use 0.0.0.0:7381. When a trusted reverse proxy is
used, bind DXWeb Admin to a private address such as 127.0.0.1 and enable
MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1 so Mojolicious uses the proxy information for the
original client address. Do not expose that private backend listener to
untrusted clients.

The administrative backend is dxweb-admin/admin.pl. It uses a local-only
DXSpider transport at 127.0.0.1 and DXS_PORT (default 27754). DXSpider
allocates its #WEB-n technical channel dynamically. Browser sessions authenticate as DXSpider users. Privilege >=5 permits
read-only access to authorized views; privilege >=9 is required for
administrative changes. Sensitive registration data is masked for priv 5.

The application exposes /healthz and /admin-version.json. The latter
reports the application version independently of the DXSpider Git build.
It also provides an asynchronous /update-status.json endpoint.

Its operation, registration, supervision, metrics, timeline and console
functions depend on the corresponding DXSpider backend capabilities.
The historical UI-V2-NOTES.txt references files from an older external
release package; this repository's installation guide is INSTALL.

For installation, see INSTALL. User Web is independent and optional.

CURRENT DEPLOYMENT AND DOCUMENTATION
------------------------------------
The reference diagrams are dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_ES.png and
dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_EN.png. Direct listeners use 7380/7381;
with the supplied Nginx examples, the public listeners remain 7380/7381
and the application backends move to loopback 7480/7481. Both connect
to DXSpider IntMsg on 127.0.0.1:27754 by default.

Current access: authenticated DXUser privilege >=5 can use permitted
read-only supervision views; administrative changes require privilege >=9.
Sensitive registration information is restricted by backend authorization.
The spots display preferences are browser-local and separated by callsign
and application, not synchronized between browsers or devices.
